{"runId":"2026-10-31T16-18-25-488Z","seq":19,"at":"2026-10-31T16:20:03.963Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C003-CH1-R0365","version":1},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Proposed go/no-go: the best-supported explanation must reproduce site-observed location and fracture features in at least two held-out joints under representative 2–6 °C service exposure, with repeatable controlled contrasts resolving claimed interactions.","sources":[],"explanation":"Two matching joints could satisfy this rule despite many nonmatching specimens, while “repeatable” and the treatment of ambiguous fracture matches have no defined acceptance rule, permitting false acceptance of an explanation. Make acceptance conditional on prespecifying the held-out denominator and exposure, specimen-level matching and uncertain-label rules, and a confidence-bound or equivalent decision rule for the claimed contrasts before held-out testing.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T16-18-25-488Z","seq":20,"at":"2026-10-31T16:20:11.563Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-review-C001-CH1-R1008","version":1},"kind":"review","inputs":[{"artifactId":"proposal-C001-CH1-R1008","version":1}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-review-C001-CH1-R1008.v1.json"}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T16-18-25-488Z","seq":21,"at":"2026-10-31T16:20:11.564Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C001-CH1-R1008","version":1},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Use representative per-site Modbus and BACnet archives, treated as unlabelled, plus safely injected bench anomalies.","sources":[],"explanation":"The held-out bench challenge lacks specified anomaly families and operating conditions, so repeated easy anomalies could yield 80% detection without meaningfully testing the proposed protocol coverage. Add a short prerequisite to agree and freeze a protocol-specific challenge matrix, episode boundaries and repetition allocation before tuning, keeping its labelled outcomes unavailable for configuration selection.","owner":"proposal_writer"},{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Proposed go/no-go targets for whichever configuration is selected: at least 80% injected-episode detection within 60 seconds, an upper 95% confidence bound of at most one false-alert episode per observed site-day, compliance with agreed device budgets, and no measurable forwarding-latency increase under matched load. Require plant managers to correctly explain four of five sampled alerts in plain language.","sources":[],"explanation":"Detection has no stated uncertainty-based acceptance rule, separate protocol reporting does not require both protocols to pass, and explanation-test sampling and correctness are undefined; small, pooled or selectively sampled results could therefore receive false approval. Require each protocol to meet the relevant gates, state a detection confidence-bound rule, and pre-agree random alert sampling and a plain-language correctness rubric, with insufficient evidence remaining a no-go.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T16-18-25-488Z","seq":22,"at":"2026-10-31T16:20:16.322Z","type":"artifact.saved","details":{"subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-review-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},"kind":"review","inputs":[{"artifactId":"proposal-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1}],"file":"artifacts/proposal-review-C009-CH1-R0288.v1.json"}}
{"runId":"2026-10-31T16-18-25-488Z","seq":23,"at":"2026-10-31T16:20:16.323Z","type":"critic.revise","details":{"phase":"proposal","subject":{"artifactId":"proposal-C009-CH1-R0288","version":1},"issues":[{"category":"plan_underspecified","severity":"blocking","claim":"Proposed go/no-go: upper 95% uncertainty bounds below 5% in both populations, no precision regression, automatic handling of inflections/script mixing, and a simulated quarterly update preserving these results without full re-indexing.","sources":[{"recordId":"C009-CH1","field":"detail","quote":"A good outcome is getting that 18% miss rate below 5% and keeping it there with a manageable maintenance process.","datasetVersion":"einstein-matchmaker-data@4fb99b3"}],"explanation":"The confidence-bound rule covers miss rates, but the separate precision gate has no statistical acceptance condition, so sampling noise could permit acceptance despite a real relevance regression. Add a prerequisite to agree a precision non-inferiority margin and require the lower confidence bound on the paired precision difference to exceed its negative, both before and after the update replay.","owner":"proposal_writer"}]}}
